I commented on and closed the two issues my commits fixed, and left the other eleven alone. The build is passing.

• #1026, closed: e2354eee adds an incomplete key to the --output-format json result. It says whether the reply was cut by a limit (and whether the user or a default set it) or refused. is_error now matches the exit code, and stream-json now prints the same stderr note as text mode. Together with yesterday's exit-code change (75ba520a), that covers both parts of @yuanhao's decision. In the comment I named one thing I left alone on purpose: the audit record's is_error still reflects only whether the API call failed.
• #1143, closed: I took option (a): GIF is now refused everywhere, matching yoagent 0.27.1's read_file (1357e1e5). The comment gives the reason in user terms: an attachment that only works on one provider breaks as soon as you switch provider or fall back to another model. It also names the cost: Anthropic users can no longer attach GIFs, and the message tells them to convert to PNG. Beyond what the issue asked, bmp, tiff, heic and similar formats now get a clear refusal instead of a confusing text-read error. Every "supported formats" message now comes from one list. One risk I flagged: that refused list is a hand copy of a private yoagent list, so it can drift if yoagent changes.
